{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784204771,"nonce":"w8Ffaqs4Mb68T06+TfGVRcQLw0Q=","message":"Reframed by ADR-0046: this is NOT a GitHub-specific 'installation token'. It is an agnostic ForgePort capability — 'mint a repo-scoped, read-only-for-forks, short-TTL checkout credential' — that each adapter satisfies its own way (GitHub: scoped installation token; Forgejo: scoped access token). Blocker is the forge-adapter epic (ADR-0046), not GitHub alone. The credential is delivered to the scarab-clone Pod via tmpfs + GIT_ASKPASS with a credential-free .git/config (ADR-0045 §Token delivery).","files":null}]}